@startuml seq_sft_engage_rolling
title SC-SFT-02 - Drive engagement N -> D while rolling

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-SFT-006, SYS-SFT-005, SYS-SFT-001, SYS-SEL-005, SIM-PLT-002, SG-02
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
Ratios 3.06 / 1.63 / 1.00 / 0.70, final drive 3.23, tyre radius 0.31 m (system_context section 4.1).
end note

note over TCU: mode Normal, selector N, vehicle coasting above standstill (example 100 km/h)
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 2 (N), Throttle;\nSIM_Speed: OutputShaftSpeed (100 km/h)
TCU -> TCU : prepared gear = schedule gear within the 6000 rpm limit\n(SYS-SEL-005, SYS-SFT-005)
note right of TCU: prediction = OutputShaftSpeed x ratio of the new gear;\nat 100 km/h 1st gives about 8460 rpm > 6000 rpm,\nso no gear below 2nd (SYS-SFT-005 verification)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A / SS_B of the prepared gear
note right of TCU: the gear selected when the schedule gear itself exceeds\nthe limit is not named (open question N-11 in system_design.md)

User -> Console : select D
Console -> Plant : selector D
Plant -> Plant : lever in D: engages the prepared gear at once (SIM-PLT-002)
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 3 (D)
... 50 ms unchanged (SYS-SEL-001) ...
TCU -> TCU : D selected above standstill -> command the gear of the shift schedule\nwithin the limit of SYS-SFT-005 (SYS-SFT-006, SYS-SFT-001)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: same SS_A / SS_B (prepared gear taken over, no shift)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: SelectorState = 3 (D), GearTarget = prepared gear (2, 3 or 4)

note over Plant, TCU
Safe state of SG-02: no gear whose predicted input shaft speed exceeds 6000 rpm is engaged.
Later shifts follow SYS-SFT-001 .. SYS-SFT-004 (SC-SFT-03, SC-SFT-04).
end note
@enduml
